meta {
  name: entry rematch
  type: http
  seq: 20
}

post {
  url: {{collection_url}}/internal/rematch-entries
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 202
  res.body.status: eq started
}

docs {
  Entry rematch, CronJob-scheduled and operator-runnable any time: sweeps auto-priced game-backed
  entries grouped by (game, platform, region), re-resolves each triple
  whose entries sit on an unmatched or cross-region member, and
  repoints those entries to the region-correct sibling member
  (snapshot fields re-derive from it). Entries on class-compatible
  members are skipped, and user-picked matches
  (match_provenance=user) are never swept at all. Rollout
  order for region-correct pricing: deploy, then run this rematch
  (it mints missing JP/PAL members with day-zero price snapshots),
  then the catalog refresh prices them onward. Idempotent: a second run
  repoints 0.

  Answers 202 and detaches (mirrors the catalog refresh): a day-one
  backfill resolves at the provider's polite rate, which would
  otherwise outlive the write timeout. The three counts - triples
  seen, triples failed, entries repointed - no longer ride this
  response; they land in the collection service's "rematch-entries
  complete" log line and the vg.collection.rematch.* metrics instead.
  Each repoint is separately logged (entry, from, to, region): the
  audit trail for reviewing or hand-reversing a run. Single-flight: an
  overlapping trigger answers 409 rematch_in_progress.

  Guard: admin role or a service token. The bearer behind
  {{access_token}} must be an admin - the folder's dev-token flow logs
  in as alice by default, so run it with body {"user": "admin"} first,
  or override --env-var access_token with a minted admin or service
  token.
}
